{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ExplicitAlphaKH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ExplicitAlphaKH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.explicit_alpha_k_h3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.explicit_alpha_k_h3","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**Proposition (explicit α_k at H_3)**.\n\n`α_0 = 1`, `α_1 = 0`, `α_2 = z²`, `α_3 = h · z² + z`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:explicit-alpha-k-h3","label":"prop:explicit-alpha-k-h3","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.h_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.h_def","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.h","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The amplitude `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.z_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.z_def","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.z","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z = q³/(q² + 1)`, pinned by the\ndivision-free relation `z · (q + q⁻¹) = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.q","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The substrate parameter `q`, a unit of `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HeckeQ","kind":"structure","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h3.lean#L71-L86","doc":"Markov parameter `z` and amplitude `h` at substrate `q`,\npolymorphic in the ground ring `R`.\n\n`z` is the convention-D Markov parameter `q³/(q² + 1)`, pinned by\nthe division-free relation `z · (q + q⁻¹) = q²`; and `h = q - q⁻¹`\nwith the units inverse.  No square root is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}